  "investigation_notes": "Uploads outage caused by paused database dependency \u2014 not app storage.\n\n**Root cause: `incidentlab-db-1` is Paused:**\n- `incidentlab-db-1` state `paused`, status `Up 12 seconds (Paused)` while `incidentlab-app-1` is `running Up 6 seconds` (E1).\n- Inspect confirms: `status: paused`, `running: true`, `exit_code: 0`, `oom_killed: false` (E6). App itself is `running: true`, `exit_code: 0`, `oom_killed: false`, `restart_count: 0` (E5), so app did not crash/OOM.\n- Docker events show explicit cause: `incidentlab-db-1 action: pause` at `2026-10-28T23:59:08+00:00` (E7), after `health_status: healthy` at `23:59:05` (E7). Current db `health: unhealthy` (E6).\n- DB process itself was ready: `database system is ready to accept connections` (E4), so failure is pause freezing all processes, not Postgres crash/shutdown. No `die` with non-zero exit after pause (E7).\n\n**Symptoms in app (effects, not cause):**\n- `/health` returns `503 {\"status\":\"unhealthy\"}` (E2).\n- App logs: `POST /upload 500 Internal Server Error` and `GET /health 503` both with `psycopg.errors.ConnectionTimeout: connection timeout expired` in `psycopg.connect(DATABASE_URL...)` at `main.py:65 upload` and `main.py:113 health` (E3).\n\n**Ruled out:**\n- Disk/full inodes: `/srv/lab-data` `use_percent: 9.0`, `available_mb: 410.6`, `inode_use_percent: 0.2` (E8); `/` `use_percent: 6.8`, `inode_use_percent: 1.5` (E9).\n- Permissions/mount: `/srv/lab-data/uploads` `is_dir:true`, `owner 1000:1000`, `mode 0755`, `app_uid 1000`, `app_user_can_write:true` (E10); parent `/srv/lab-data` same writable (E11); app mount `source:/srv/lab-data destination:/data rw:true`, `user:1000:1000` (E5).\n- Network isolation / config change: both containers on `incidentlab_default` (E5, E6), app started after db `start` at `23:59:06` (E7) with same bind/volume as before.\n- No restart loop: both `restart_count:0` (E5, E6).\n\nRepair requires human approval: `docker unpause incidentlab-db-1`, then verify `pg_isready` healthy and app `/health` 200 and test upload.\n",
